   $q$A small plane flies with airspeed 300 mph heading due north while a wind blows due east at 40 mph. To the nearest mile per hour, what is the plane's ground speed?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$260$ mph","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-speeds"},{"text":"$340$ mph","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-speeds"},{"text":"$297$ mph","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-squares"},{"text":"$303$ mph","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$303$ mph$q$, $q$The ground velocity is $\langle 40, 300 \rangle$, so the ground speed is $\sqrt{40^2 + 300^2} = \sqrt{91600} \approx 303$ mph. The choice $340$ mph adds the speeds, which is only right when the wind blows in the direction of travel.$q$, 'draft', null)
